  "dateAssessment": "Working dates use session YAML, May 16–18, 1749 DR. The transcript names no calendar date but supports both overnight transitions; the first is a completed long rest, while the second establishes a next morning without rest credit. The opening continues session 105’s vine scouting and escape (105 u3161–u3179 → 106 u0040–u0052), with a new direct sunset anchor. Session 107 intervenes as a narrative-only session: its registered prepared source u0011–u0012 explicitly resumes this same Milo-captained beach landing in the afternoon of May 18. That retrospectively dates the landing; it does not independently time every preceding preparation. Session 107 then explores inland and reaches the Wanderer site; session 108 opens with further climbing and scouting there (108 u0017–u0032), not at session 106’s beach. The two-hour correction supersedes the earlier four-hour scouting claim.",
